 and $\\mathbf{b}=12\\mathbf{i}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059523 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1d2717f9-b905-59eb-85d7-6db4f9c9dc7f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059523 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute $\\mathbf{a}-2\\mathbf{b}$, we just need to compute all of the $\\mathbf{i}$'s and $\\mathbf{j}$'s, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - 2b &= (-4i + 6j) - 2(12i) \\\\\n&=-4i + 6j - 24i \\\\\n&= (-4i - 24i) + 6j \\\\\n&=-28i + 6j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059524 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4293" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059524 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle -7, 15 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 14, -11 \\rangle$. Find $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059524 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2cb63c87-320a-5cb4-b413-8c6bf9723641" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059524 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute $\\mathbf{a}-3\\mathbf{b}$, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na - 3b &= ⟨ - 7, 15⟩ - 3 \\cdot ⟨14,-11⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 7, 15⟩ - ⟨42,-33⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 7 - 42, 15 - (-33)⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 49, 48⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059525 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4294" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059525 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$ $\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $2\\mathbf{a}-(\\mathbf{b}-5\\mathbf{c})$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059525 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "43cfef07-255d-5167-b815-267883918993" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059525 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a - (b - 5c) &= 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} - (\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} - 5 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} - (\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix} - \\begin{bmatrix}17 \\\\ -31\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 21\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059526 #edb/ref 1069 "e-4295" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059526 #edb/ref 1071 "The vectors $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ are given in the picture below. Find the coordinates of $\\vec{a}+6\\vec{b}$.\n\n![](images/56/56b10e759084da6fb21c8421bc9ff6d74aac2602df28f6c8e478bd874d7d6e9f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059526 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0adf8fad-9a6f-5eb1-970f-11633ba98ca1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059526 #edb/ref 1074 "From the picture, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\vec{a}=\\langle -3,2 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\vec{b}=\\langle 4,5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, to compute the result, we just need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na^(→) + 6b^(→) &= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + 6 \\cdot ⟨4, 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨6 \\cdot 4, 6 \\cdot 5⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨ - 3, 2⟩ + ⟨24, 30⟩ \\\\\n&= ⟨21, 32⟩\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060393 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186233365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186509348 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186509350 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186509352 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186509354 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186509362 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186059710 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186509365 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [1759218